{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/eb8dcz","slide":5,"text":"/Users/al3x3n0/huawei/osrec/runtime/aarch64_gateway.c\n/Users/al3x3n0/huawei/osrec/include/osrec/aarch64_frame.h\n/Users/al3x3n0/huawei/osrec/include/osrec/syscall_slice.h\n\nLinux ABI uses x8 as syscall number, x0–x5 for arguments and x0 for the result. The port defines the ABI. Declared SVCs are patched to BRKs. The gateway validates the expected route and ordinal, invokes selected original syscall bodies with reviewed models and resumes at original SVC PC + 4."}
